; Regression: a statement missing its block reported K0100 ("expected `{`") at the next token,
; and the enclosing block then reported K0122 for the junk run starting at exactly the same
; span. `for x in = 1` even got two K0122 there. One gap gets one diagnostic (grammar.md §19.4,
; diagnostics.md): the junk run's K0122 is dropped when it repeats the span just reported.
(SourceFile
  (FuncDecl func f (ParamList)
    (Block
      (DoStmt do) (ErrorNode =) (Literal 1)
      (WhileStmt while (NameExpr a)) (ErrorNode =) (Literal 1)
      (ForStmt for (IdentPattern x) in) (ErrorNode =) (Literal 1))))
